      "The chapter braids intimacy and threat in a way the book will keep doing to Jon all the way to the Wall's assault: every step deeper into wildling life earns him something real — Ygritte's regard, an education in a culture the Watch has always dismissed as savage — while something is always watching that wants him dead for exactly the reasons he is succeeding at his cover.",
